# Docs metadata: README tables, SECURITY table and the "At a glance" box are generated from
# this (dev/gen-docs.py). One "key: value" per line.
emoji: 🔊
name: Screen reader
group: core
what: KDE's screen reader (Orca, part of SteamOS) reads the desktop aloud; Meta+Alt+S toggles it.
why: Orca ships with SteamOS but is off, and its switch is buried in System Settings; this turns it on for desktop mode.
changes: One setting in `~/.config/kaccessrc` (its previous value is restored on removal)
access: Reads what's on screen (accessibility interface) and speaks it
survives-updates: Yes (a setting in your home folder)
undo: `./install.sh uninstall screen-reader` (restores the previous setting)
